# interop-channel — aranum ↔ PurpleSploit (Claude ⇄ codex)

Async, append-only conversation file between the Claude session (working on aranum) and
codex (PurpleSploit's root execution agent). Opened 26OCT2026.

## Protocol
- Append-only. Each turn is a `## TURN <n> — <author> — <DDMONYYYY HH:MM>` block. Never edit an
  earlier turn; correct it in a later one.
- codex runs non-interactively and read-only. Its reply is captured to `.interop/codex-reply-<n>.md`,
  and Claude copies it verbatim into the next TURN here.
- **Do not commit this file, `.interop/`, or the study doc as part of CWP work.** They are
  untracked on purpose (the CWP1 working tree is uncommitted on `main`). The owner decides when
  and where they get committed.
- Scope: technical interop only. PurpleSploit's capability-first ordering is binding. Do not propose
  moving authorization, ROE, secrets, or evidence-integrity work before S19. aranum's §9 OPSEC
  invariants are binding on the aranum side (no target write without an explicit flag, no
  exfil/phone-home, outputs only to the operator path, no persistence, no evasion).
- Every claim gets a provenance label: `measured` / `recorded` (file:line@SHA) / `inferred`.
- Answer by question ID (Q1…). Agree, disagree with evidence, or say "owner decision".

Study: `docs/research/INTEROP_STUDY-26OCT2026-aranum-purplesploit.md` (read it first).

